1
00:04:37,500 --> 00:04:43,500
A real horror story…

2
00:09:15,000 --> 00:09:21,000
The Night Stalker is a mystery, horror, thriller
film directed by John Llewellyn Moxey.

3
00:13:52,500 --> 00:13:58,500
Wisecracking reporter Carl Kolchak investigates a string of murders
in Las Vegas and suspects the culprit is a vampire.

4
00:18:30,000 --> 00:18:36,000
His editor thinks he's crazy and the police think he's a
nuisance, so Kolchak takes matters into his own hands.

5
00:23:07,500 --> 00:23:13,500
Carl Kolchak, played by Darren McGavin.

6
00:27:45,000 --> 00:27:51,000
Gail Foster, played by Carol Lynley.

7
00:32:22,500 --> 00:32:28,500
Tony Vincenzo, played by Simon Oakland.

8
00:37:00,000 --> 00:37:06,000
Bernie Jenks, played by Ralph Meeker.

9
00:41:37,500 --> 00:41:43,500
Sheriff Warren A. Butcher, played by Claude Akins.

10
00:46:15,000 --> 00:46:21,000
Police Chief Ed Masterson, played by Charles McGraw.

11
00:50:52,500 --> 00:50:58,500
The Night Stalker is an American made-for-television horror film which aired
on ABC on January 11, 1972, as their ABC Movie of the Week.

12
00:55:30,000 --> 00:55:36,000
In the film, Carl Kolchak (Darren McGavin), an investigative reporter, comes to
suspect that a serial killer in the Las Vegas area is actually a vampire.

13
01:00:07,500 --> 01:00:13,500
The Night Stalker set a record for the most viewed made-for-TV film.

14
01:04:45,000 --> 01:04:51,000
It was followed by a sequel, The Night Strangler, and a television series, Kolchak: The
Night Stalker, both of which had McGavin reprise his role as Carl Kolchak.

15
01:09:22,500 --> 01:09:28,500
The tone is intense and dark and mind_bending.
